WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.708 --> 00:00:36.208
In verse 14.10, Lord Krishna explains
that the three gunas –

2
00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:38.791
sattva, rajas, and tamas –

3
00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:41.583
are in a constant struggle for
dominance within the jivatma.

4
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:43.458
He has already described their effects

5
00:00:43.458 --> 00:00:46.458
in detail in the previous verses.

6
00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:50.041
Based on actions, company, and diet,

7
00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:55.125
sometimes one guna becomes dominant,
sometimes another.

8
00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:58.250
The soul is eternal and beyond the gunas,

9
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.333
but because of this inner struggle,

10
00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.583
instability is experienced in life.

11
00:01:04.583 --> 00:01:06.208
This verse makes clear

12
00:01:06.208 --> 00:01:08.291
that the gunas are not permanent.

13
00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:10.750
They keep changing.

14
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:14.541
Therefore the aim of spiritual practice

15
00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.666
is to rise above them.

16
00:01:21.208 --> 00:01:23.041
Lord Krishna says

17
00:01:23.041 --> 00:01:26.625
that sattva, rajas, and tamas do
not remain constant.

18
00:01:26.625 --> 00:01:29.416
They are in continuous competition.

19
00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:33.916
Sometimes sattva rises, sometimes rajas,
sometimes tamas.

20
00:01:33.916 --> 00:01:35.333
Whichever guna rises

21
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:38.125
suppresses the other two.

22
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:41.083
Our thoughts, emotions,

23
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:44.666
and actions are all affected by this
shifting influence.

24
00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:48.958
For example – many people are
enthusiastic starters.

25
00:01:48.958 --> 00:01:50.416
Under sattva’s influence,

26
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:52.666
they begin a good work –

27
00:01:52.666 --> 00:01:54.458
say, teaching children

28
00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:58.458
in a poor neighbourhood on their days off.

29
00:01:58.458 --> 00:02:02.208
Their mind is clear and motivated.

30
00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:03.166
But then

31
00:02:03.166 --> 00:02:05.083
rajas comes in

32
00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.083
and the mind starts to drift –

33
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:08.541
they begin to want

34
00:02:08.541 --> 00:02:10.833
everyone to know about it,

35
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:12.708
photographs in the press,

36
00:02:12.708 --> 00:02:15.291
awards for social service.

37
00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:16.583
And finally

38
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.791
tamas brings laziness and disinterest,

39
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:24.083
and after a little publicity and recognition,

40
00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:27.375
they gradually stop going to the children’s

41
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:30.916
settlement altogether.

42
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:34.708
This is why life has its ups and downs.

43
00:02:34.708 --> 00:02:37.583
Sometimes you are enthusiastic and active,

44
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:40.958
sometimes sluggish and drained.

45
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:43.125
The gunas influence not only actions

46
00:02:43.125 --> 00:02:44.833
but also the lens

47
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:46.500
through which success is seen.

48
00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.166
In sattva, success

49
00:02:48.166 --> 00:02:51.125
is measured by knowledge and virtue.

50
00:02:51.125 --> 00:02:55.458
In rajas, by wealth and recognition.

51
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:58.791
In tamas, even the clarity of success is lost

52
00:02:58.791 --> 00:03:01.458
and confusion sets in.

53
00:03:01.458 --> 00:03:03.125
You must understand

54
00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:04.750
that since the gunas

55
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:06.416
are constantly in conflict,

56
00:03:06.416 --> 00:03:09.375
the seeker must choose sattva

57
00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:12.916
and ultimately rise above all gunas.

58
00:03:12.916 --> 00:03:14.000
This is possible

59
00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.125
only through spiritual knowledge

60
00:03:16.125 --> 00:03:18.458
and the practice of devotion.

61
00:03:18.458 --> 00:03:20.708
When a person becomes steady

62
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:22.125
through connection with Lord Krishna,

63
00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:25.833
only then does the pull of the gunas end

64
00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:28.500
and liberation is attained.

65
00:03:33.166 --> 00:03:37.625
Have you ever experienced this – one day

66
00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:41.916
you wake up inspired and full of energy,

67
00:03:41.916 --> 00:03:43.333
and the very next day

68
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:47.083
you feel irritable or heavy?

69
00:03:47.083 --> 00:03:48.875
You wonder –

70
00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:52.125
why can I not stay stable?

71
00:03:52.125 --> 00:03:55.500
Why do my thoughts, my energy,

72
00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.833
my feelings keep changing?

73
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.250
Let Me tell you –

74
00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.583
this is not without reason.

75
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:08.041
It is the effect of prakriti’s three gunas,

76
00:04:08.041 --> 00:04:09.958
which are always

77
00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:14.666
competing with each other within.

78
00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:18.125
Sometimes sattva Guna becomes dominant –

79
00:04:18.125 --> 00:04:21.291
bringing you peace, clarity,

80
00:04:21.291 --> 00:04:23.916
and a sense of purpose.

81
00:04:23.916 --> 00:04:26.708
Sometimes Rajo Guna takes over –

82
00:04:26.708 --> 00:04:29.875
filling you with ambition, restlessness,

83
00:04:29.875 --> 00:04:33.333
and the craving to prove yourself.

84
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:36.625
And sometimes Tamo Guna

85
00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:40.208
creeps in slowly –

86
00:04:40.208 --> 00:04:45.666
making you heavy, listless, and indifferent.

87
00:04:45.666 --> 00:04:49.791
Remember – these changes are not you.

88
00:04:49.791 --> 00:04:54.666
These are gunas exerting their influence on you,

89
00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:56.041
but

90
00:04:56.041 --> 00:05:00.125
you can rise above them.

91
00:05:00.125 --> 00:05:04.250
The first step is awareness.

92
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:08.208
Start observing yourself.

93
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:12.875
Pause for a moment and ask –

94
00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:18.500
‘Which guna is influencing me right now?’

95
00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:20.708
This simple awareness alone

96
00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:24.416
will teach you to give

97
00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:28.416
a responsible response rather than
an immediate reaction.

98
00:05:28.416 --> 00:05:31.291
I have given you this knowledge

99
00:05:31.291 --> 00:05:36.333
so you do not remain a slave to your moods.

100
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:38.000
Embrace it.

101
00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:43.000
Gradually you will gain mastery
over the gunas –

102
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.333
not by fighting them,

103
00:05:45.333 --> 00:05:49.458
but by rising above them – through clarity,

104
00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:53.125
discipline, and devotion.

105
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:56.208
This is the path to steadiness,

106
00:05:56.208 --> 00:05:59.166
even as the world

107
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:01.750
keeps changing.

108
00:06:06.458 --> 00:06:09.625
When your child throws a tantrum –

109
00:06:09.625 --> 00:06:11.083
shouts in anger,

110
00:06:11.083 --> 00:06:12.666
loses focus in class,

111
00:06:12.666 --> 00:06:17.000
or becomes excessively competitive –

112
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.708
you naturally

113
00:06:18.708 --> 00:06:21.750
want to correct the behaviour.

114
00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:24.250
But pause for a moment.

115
00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:29.666
I want you to think a little more deeply.

116
00:06:29.666 --> 00:06:34.166
Do not only correct the behaviour –

117
00:06:34.166 --> 00:06:36.291
understand the guna working

118
00:06:36.291 --> 00:06:39.458
behind it.

119
00:06:39.458 --> 00:06:43.208
Just as adults are influenced by
the three gunas –

120
00:06:43.208 --> 00:06:44.291
sattva, rajas,

121
00:06:44.291 --> 00:06:46.083
and tamas –

122
00:06:46.083 --> 00:06:48.791
so are children.

123
00:06:48.791 --> 00:06:53.083
Sometimes your child is calm and thoughtful –

124
00:06:53.083 --> 00:06:55.416
this is sattva Guna at work.

125
00:06:55.416 --> 00:06:59.250
Sometimes they are restless or
overly competitive –

126
00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.333
Rajo Guna is dominant. And sometimes

127
00:07:02.333 --> 00:07:05.791
they sink into laziness or indifference –

128
00:07:05.791 --> 00:07:08.250
this is Tamo Guna’s effect.

129
00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.458
If you only react to the visible

130
00:07:10.458 --> 00:07:13.708
behaviour, you can correct

131
00:07:13.708 --> 00:07:17.666
the symptom but not the cause.

132
00:07:17.666 --> 00:07:21.125
But when you start recognising

133
00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:25.458
which guna is influencing them,

134
00:07:25.458 --> 00:07:27.916
your guidance becomes

135
00:07:27.916 --> 00:07:29.625
more compassionate

136
00:07:29.625 --> 00:07:32.166
and wise.

137
00:07:32.166 --> 00:07:35.333
Sometimes a child only needs

138
00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:37.208
a gentle nudge

139
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:39.375
toward sattva –

140
00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:41.375
through a calm conversation,

141
00:07:41.375 --> 00:07:46.250
a few moments of quietness,
or the right environment.

142
00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.916
I have given you this understanding

143
00:07:48.916 --> 00:07:53.458
so that your home is not only a
place of discipline,

144
00:07:53.458 --> 00:07:57.458
but a centre of growth.

145
00:07:57.458 --> 00:08:01.708
Help them rise –

146
00:08:01.708 --> 00:08:04.750
first by clearly seeing

147
00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.208
which guna is actually

148
00:08:07.208 --> 00:08:08.875
binding them.

149
00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.708
You may have noticed –

150
00:08:15.708 --> 00:08:18.541
sometimes you are sharp, creative,

151
00:08:18.541 --> 00:08:21.833
and focused,

152
00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.916
and sometimes you are just drifting along,

153
00:08:24.916 --> 00:08:28.166
without any clarity.

154
00:08:28.166 --> 00:08:30.500
This is not coincidence.

155
00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.750
It is the continuous struggle

156
00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:36.708
of prakriti’s three gunas – sattva, rajas,
and tamas –

157
00:08:36.708 --> 00:08:41.125
working subtly within.

158
00:08:41.125 --> 00:08:44.625
When sattva is dominant, you think clearly,

159
00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:47.875
stay creative and steady.

160
00:08:47.875 --> 00:08:50.666
Rajas pushes you constantly

161
00:08:50.666 --> 00:08:53.791
into the race for activity and results.

162
00:08:53.791 --> 00:08:56.708
Tamas slows you down,

163
00:08:56.708 --> 00:08:58.458
clouds your thinking,

164
00:08:58.458 --> 00:09:03.083
and weakens your will.

165
00:09:03.083 --> 00:09:07.125
This does not only happen to you –

166
00:09:07.125 --> 00:09:10.208
it affects the entire team.

167
00:09:10.208 --> 00:09:14.125
What you sometimes call ‘low performance’

168
00:09:14.125 --> 00:09:17.291
or ‘high energy’ is often

169
00:09:17.291 --> 00:09:18.500
simply a reflection

170
00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:21.583
of the guna active at that time.

171
00:09:21.583 --> 00:09:25.750
The work of leadership is not only
to bring results –

172
00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.791
it is also to recognise the energy

173
00:09:28.791 --> 00:09:30.791
driving them.

174
00:09:30.791 --> 00:09:34.750
And for the employee too, understanding

175
00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:35.833
the guna behind

176
00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:40.000
a leadership directive is very helpful.

177
00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.791
So both as a leader and as a team member,

178
00:09:44.791 --> 00:09:48.041
pay attention to even the subtlest

179
00:09:48.041 --> 00:09:51.041
shifts in work culture.

180
00:09:51.041 --> 00:09:53.625
Recognise your own rises and falls.

181
00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:55.916
Then create an environment

182
00:09:55.916 --> 00:09:58.625
that invites clarity –

183
00:09:58.625 --> 00:10:03.166
light, well-organised, and balanced.

184
00:10:03.166 --> 00:10:05.250
Team guidance should follow

185
00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.375
the same principle.

186
00:10:07.375 --> 00:10:09.791
A sattvic workplace

187
00:10:09.791 --> 00:10:12.041
is not a luxury –

188
00:10:12.041 --> 00:10:15.833
it is the foundation of sustained excellence.

189
00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:19.791
When you begin to understand these gunas,

190
00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:21.458
you stop reacting

191
00:10:21.458 --> 00:10:23.625
instantly.

192
00:10:23.625 --> 00:10:28.000
You respond with awareness.

193
00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.291
This is the real transformation –

194
00:10:30.291 --> 00:10:34.750
where work is no longer limited to operations,

195
00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.916
but becomes leadership

196
00:10:38.916 --> 00:10:40.708
with wisdom.

197
00:10:40.708 --> 00:10:44.541
Where a person is no longer just
an ordinary worker,

198
00:10:44.541 --> 00:10:45.416
but a

199
00:10:45.416 --> 00:10:51.041
responsible and dedicated part
of the organisation.
